Keel Skills is now permissively licensed (MIT) on purpose: the goal is for the
authorization model and the AGENT_POLICY.md format to become a shared standard
for governing AI agents, adopted and reimplemented freely.

Attribution — appreciated, and the norm we ask you to follow even though MIT
only requires you to keep the copyright notice above:

  If Keel Skills (or its model) helps your project, product, or framework,
  please keep a visible credit — "Governance model based on Keel Skills by
  Esteban Aguilar" — with a link back to the project.

The portable parts are specified, runtime-neutral, in SPEC.md:
  - the L1 / L2 / L3 authorization model and the four-step safety test;
  - the AGENT_POLICY.md configuration format.

Implementations in any agent runtime (Claude Code, Agent SDK, other harnesses)
are welcome and encouraged. If you build one, open an issue — we want to list it.
